 "remarks": "Newly renovated 3-bed, 1.5-bath home on a quiet dead-end street near downtown Greenwich. This classic New England two-story sits on a tree-lined street with a covered front porch, black metal railings, and a concrete walkway through a freshly landscaped lawn. Gray clapboard siding, white trim, and a dark shingled roof give it polished curb appeal, and the front doors under the porch add a distinctive touch. Inside, an open main level features light hardwood floors, recessed lighting, and a striking linear fireplace set into a dark stone feature wall. The kitchen is the centerpiece: light-wood and white cabinetry, full-height marble backsplash, a waterfall-edge marble island with a high-arc faucet, a Viking range, and a Sub-Zero refrigerator. A custom wooden wine rack tucks under the staircase, and a stacked washer-dryer sits in a dedicated laundry nook. There are three bedrooms and 1.5 baths. The primary suite has a double-door closet, and the bathrooms feature floating wood vanities, backlit mirrors, and a tiled shower with a rain head and a honeycomb mosaic niche. The house sits close to downtown Greenwich while offering the quieter feel of a dead-end street-recently renovated throughout and ready to move in.",
